# Notes notebook organization source study

The selected original behavior comes from Laurent Cozic and the Joplin contributors, released Joplin Desktop v3.6.14, commit 7e2765a3857754d12dbadea442b60ceaf9d4b23d. The original root LICENSE states AGPL-3.0-or-later except when a subdirectory supplies a different license. The retained packages/lib/package.json likewise declares AGPL-3.0-or-later; the inspected ancestor license locations had no override. Exact upstream source/license and response bytes, including failed requests, are retained under original/ with .snapshot extensions and SHA-256 provenance.

The test-only notebook-original-oracle.mjs extracts and executes original Folder and Note methods. Those original method slices remain subject to the upstream license, copyright and attribution. Candidate runtime modules are new source-assisted implementations of the selected contracts. This study makes no clean-room or MIT derivation claim and does not determine a broader distribution license for the repository. Preserve upstream notices and review the applicable license obligations before publishing original implementation material.

The old 22-check JEX serialization evidence remains bound to its historical c17c205049ce74e449dc1ce08cbd1c875410d7d5 source epoch; it is not evidence that the entire released Desktop 3.6.14 product was executed. The notebook oracle is a bounded helper experiment, not a complete original application wrapper.
